sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Consumer as SDK Consumer
    participant Config as CKKSConfig
    participant Session as HESession
    participant Resolver as Backend Resolver
    participant Guard as Native Runtime Guard
    participant Adapter as OpenFHEBackend / FidesBackend
    participant Native as Native HE Runtime

    Consumer->>Config: profile("ckks-balanced-v1")
    Config->>Config: validate CKKS parameters
    Config-->>Consumer: CKKSConfig + fingerprint

    Consumer->>Session: create(device or backend, config)
    Session->>Resolver: create_backend(selection, config)
    Resolver->>Resolver: normalize cpu/openfhe or gpu/fides

    alt No backend explicitly selected
        Resolver->>Resolver: detect installed backend components
        alt Exactly one backend is installed
            Resolver->>Guard: claim_native_runtime(detected backend)
        else None or both are installed
            Resolver-->>Consumer: BackendUnavailableError
        end
    else Backend explicitly selected
        Resolver->>Guard: claim_native_runtime(selected backend)
    end

    alt Process has no selected native runtime
        Guard->>Guard: store selected backend for process lifetime
        Guard-->>Resolver: accepted
    else Same backend already selected
        Guard-->>Resolver: accepted
    else Different backend already selected
        Guard-->>Consumer: BackendUnavailableError
    end

    Resolver->>Adapter: construct(config)
    Adapter->>Native: initialize context and keys
    Native-->>Adapter: context ID, key-bundle ID, engine version
    Adapter-->>Session: backend instance
    Session-->>Consumer: HESession

    Consumer->>Session: capabilities
    Session-->>Consumer: backend, scheme, operations and feature flags

    Consumer->>Session: close()
    Session->>Adapter: close()
    Adapter->>Native: clear native resources
    Session-->>Consumer: None

    Note over Guard,Native: close() does not reset the process runtime claim.<br/>Start a fresh Python process to change CPU/GPU backend.
    Note over Adapter,Native: OpenFHE also permits only one active local<br/>OpenFHE HESession because evaluation-key state is process-global.
